content.text:
The panic is in `Parse` at the first line of the body:

```go
unit := s[len(s)-1]
```

For an empty string, `len(s)` is 0, so the index is `-1`, which produces the `index out of range [-1]` panic. The function never checks for empty input before indexing.

The fix is an early check that returns an error:

```go
func Parse(s string) (Duration, error) {
	if len(s) == 0 {
		return 0, fmt.Errorf("duration: empty string")
	}
	unit := s[len(s)-1]
	// ...
}
```

This file is also incomplete. The body ends at `// ...` with no return statement, so it wouldn't compile as shown. It may be an excerpt. The `Duration` type and the rest of the parsing logic aren't visible, so I can't check whether other inputs cause problems. If you can share the rest of the function or the file that defines `Duration`, I can look at those next.
